  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_009: multimodal/scgpt/ViT-L/transformer/concat at 0.507 acc, 3.95 GPU-hrs), the largest source of uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes meaningful signal. config_001 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is a clean ablation that removes only the image branch while keeping the same RNA encoder and aggregation. If accuracy drops substantially, the image modality is essential and I should keep investing in multimodal configs; if it stays close, I can redirect the remaining 8 experiments toward cheaper RNA-only or lighter multimodal variants. This single experiment resolves the most impactful architectural question and directly informs all subsequent choices. Expected relative cost: ~2.0–2.5 GPU hours (roughly 55–65% of config_009), since it retains scgpt + transformer aggregation but eliminates ViT-L image encoding and fusion, saving significant compute for the remaining budget."
}

